cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the U.S. Harmonized Vital Statistics resource, please cite the relevant subproject deposit(s) below."
title: "U.S. Harmonized Vital Statistics Microdata"
abstract: >
  A unified resource integrating harmonized U.S. natality, linked birth–infant death, fetal death, and matched-multiples
  (twins/triplets/quadruplets) public-use microdata released by the National Center for Health Statistics (NCHS) into
  stable parquet column schemas spanning multiple Standard Certificate revisions and NCHS layout reformats. Each product
  is validated against every per-year figure NCHS publishes in the relevant National Vital Statistics Reports series
  (or against documentation Table 1 cells in the case of matched multiples).
authors:
  - family-names: Plutchok
    given-names: Yoel
license: CC-BY-4.0
type: dataset
keywords:
  - vital statistics
  - natality
  - fetal death
  - stillbirth
  - linked birth-infant death
  - matched multiples
  - twins
  - perinatal epidemiology
  - National Vital Statistics System
  - NCHS
  - data harmonization
  - public use microdata
  - United States
